# Zensim parameter sweep validation results
# Date: 2026-03-08
# Encoder: jxl-encoder-rs (feat/metric-loops branch, commit 87f620a)
# Zensim: 499c811 (HF features) + 1bd4695 (docs update)
# Dataset: 2 CLIC 2025 (1024×1024) + 2 CID22 (512×512), d=1.0 and d=2.0
# Modes: e7 (baseline), e7-zen (zensim 4 iters), e8-zen (bfly 2 + zen 4)
#
# Three configs compared:
#   defaults: masking=4, sqrt=1, hf=1, alpha=0.20, factor=1.15
#   optimal:  masking=8, sqrt=0, hf=1, alpha=0.30, factor=1.15
#   alt:      masking=8, sqrt=0, hf=1, alpha=0.25, factor=1.15
#
# Results (relative to e7 baseline, averaged over 4 images × 2 distances):
#
#   Config     | e7-zen4          | e8-zen4
#              | ΔSize%   ΔSS2    | ΔSize%   ΔSS2
#   -----------|------------------|------------------
#   defaults   | +1.22%  +0.780  | -3.97%  +0.134
#   optimal    | +0.49%  +0.928  | -4.88%  -0.059
#   alt (new)  | +0.50%  +0.922  | -4.67%  +0.041
#
# Selected: "alt" config as new defaults
#   - e7-zen4: 19% more SSIM2 gain, 60% less size inflation
#   - e8-zen4: 0.7pp more size savings while maintaining SSIM2
#
# Key findings from 3-phase sweep:
#   Phase 1 (24 configs): sqrt=0 universally better, masking=8 best
#   Phase 2 (29 configs): alpha=0.25-0.30, factor_max=1.10-1.15 optimal
#   Phase 3: not completed (script bug), using defaults for norm/spatial_w
